.SH NAME
ssoossh-host-mapping-list - Print the current principal mapping.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh host mapping list [flags] [args]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the mapping file named by --file as YAML, in the form it is stored in, so the output can be redirected back into a file. Prints nothing when the mapping is empty or the file does not exist yet.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to an extra config file, merged after the standard locations

.PP
\fB--file\fP="/etc/ssoossh/principals.yaml"
	path to the local principal mapping file (YAML: local account -> list of principals)

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address, e.g. https://ssh.example.com; https is assumed when no scheme is given

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


